      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Inyotef|400208\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Jni̯-jtj=f-ꜥꜣ.w reads as the signs j, n, i̯, j, t, j, f, ꜥ, ꜣ, w. In 'Inyotef' the initial I matches the first j, n matches n, y matches i̯, and the o is an extra vowel. The t matches t, the e is an extra vowel (the second j may be left out), and f matches f. That covers 'Inyotef' = Jni̯-jtj=f. The final element ꜥꜣ.w ('aa') is not represented at all. The ꜥ and ꜣ would each need a vowel letter after the f, and Inyotef ends with f and has no letters left. Two signs, ꜥ and ꜣ, therefore have nothing to represent them, and the element count differs (three elements against one). Record 1 is the name Inyotef (Intef) alone, and record 2 is the different name Inyotef-aa.\"}"
